From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] boot: cedit: redraw only after an action

cedit_run() renders the expo on every pass of its loop, and expo_poll()
returns -EAGAIN after ~20 ms when no key arrives. So the whole screen is
filled with the background and redrawn about 50 times a second while the
form just sits there. On the Lctech Pi F1C200s, whose display engine
scans the buffer U-Boot draws into, that shows as a constant vertical
flicker.

Render once at the start and again only after an action. Nothing in the
scene changes without one.

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
---
--- a/boot/cedit.c
+++ b/boot/cedit.c
@@ -202,6 +202,7 @@
 	struct udevice *dev;
 	struct scene *scn;
 	uint scene_id;
+	bool redraw;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = uclass_first_device_err(UCLASS_VIDEO, &dev);
@@ -216,18 +217,30 @@
 
 	exp->done = false;
 	exp->save = false;
+	redraw = true;
 	do {
 		struct expo_action act;
 
-		ret = expo_render(exp);
-		if (ret)
-			return log_msg_ret("cer", ret);
+		/*
+		 * expo_poll() gives up after ~20 ms without a key. Rendering
+		 * on every pass fills and redraws the whole screen ~50 times
+		 * a second, which a display that scans the drawing buffer
+		 * shows as constant flicker; only an action changes the scene.
+		 */
+		if (redraw) {
+			ret = expo_render(exp);
+			if (ret)
+				return log_msg_ret("cer", ret);
+			redraw = false;
+		}
 
 		ret = expo_poll(exp, &act);
-		if (!ret)
+		if (!ret) {
 			cedit_do_action(exp, scn, vid_priv, &act);
-		else if (ret != -EAGAIN)
+			redraw = true;
+		} else if (ret != -EAGAIN) {
 			return log_msg_ret("cep", ret);
+		}
 	} while (!exp->done);
 
 	if (ret)
